Before going out, I video call my family in Mexico.
On the screen are my parents, my younger sister Sofia, and my older brother Diego.
They all happily sing a birthday song for me together.
From the background, our dog Lola barks loudly.
I laugh and say, "Lola, how are you?"
My mother asks, "Maya, has our parcel reached Mumbai?"
I reply, "Yes mom, it arrived yesterday afternoon."
"I put it on the table last night."
"But I have not opened it yet."
My father asks, "What is your plan for this evening?"
I say, "I will celebrate with my friends this evening."
This is my first birthday away from home.
For the first time, I am celebrating my birthday without my family.
Diego and Sofia say, "We miss you a lot."
I smile and say, "I miss you all a lot too."
Now I have to leave for the office.
I say goodbye to everyone and hang up the phone.
